{
  "_doc": "General F1 tech (regulation level) per Car Explorer component, Pirelli tyre facts and power-unit maker facts. Statements are normalised in our own words; every one keeps its source. Rendered as GENERAL F1 TECH, never as a team-specific spec. Upstream data hosts are provenance-only (not linked on pages).",
  "version": "f1-tech-2026@1",
  "season": 2026,
  "retrieved": "2026-10-02",
  "conflicts": [
    "MGU-K recovery: Mercedes/McLaren/Alpine sheets say 9 MJ/lap; FIA Section C Issue 20 C5.2.10 and FIA 2024 release say 8.5 MJ/lap. Use FIA for general text.",
    "Min mass: FIA 2024 release 768 kg; Issue 20 C4.1 = 724 kg (726 kg quali) + nominal tyre mass. Team-published weights 770 (Audi, Haas), 772 (Mercedes, McLaren, Alpine), 772.4 (Williams, media).",
    "Active aero naming: FIA 2024 release 'Z-Mode/X-Mode'; regulations + teams use 'Corner Mode/Straight Mode' (McLaren says 'Cornering Mode').",
    "Red Bull RB22 page labels 185 kg as 'chassis weight' - it is the PU minimum weight."
  ],
  "general": {
    "front-wing": [
      {
        "text": "The front wing carries two adjustable flaps (primary and secondary) that the FIA standard ECU switches between two fixed positions: Corner Mode (high downforce) and Straight Mode (reduced incidence, low drag).",
        "sources": [
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/system/files/documents/fia_2026_f1_regulations_-_section_c_technical_-_iss_20_-_2026-08-05.pdf",
            "publisher": "FIA - 2026 F1 Regulations Section C [Technical] Issue 20",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2026-08-05"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Each switch between modes must complete within 400 ms, and any system failure must return the wing to Corner Mode.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/system/files/documents/fia_2026_f1_regulations_-_section_c_technical_-_iss_20_-_2026-08-05.pdf",
            "publisher": "FIA - 2026 F1 Regulations Section C [Technical] Issue 20",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2026-08-05"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The front wing flaps may only be deployed (Straight Mode) when the car is stationary or fully inside a designated Activation Zone.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/system/files/documents/fia_2026_f1_regulations_-_section_c_technical_-_iss_20_-_2026-08-05.pdf",
            "publisher": "FIA - 2026 F1 Regulations Section C [Technical] Issue 20",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2026-08-05"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The 2026 front wing is about 100 mm narrower than the 2022-25 design. Early FIA material called the modes 'Z-Mode'/'X-Mode'; the regulations now use Corner Mode / Straight Mode.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/news/new-era-competition-fia-showcases-future-focused-formula-1-regulations-2026-and-beyond",
            "publisher": "FIA",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2024-06-06"
          },
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/system/files/documents/fia_2026_f1_regulations_-_section_c_technical_-_iss_20_-_2026-08-05.pdf",
            "publisher": "FIA - 2026 F1 Regulations Section C [Technical] Issue 20",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2026-08-05"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "rear-wing": [
      {
        "text": "The rear wing flap has two fixed, ECU-commanded positions - Corner Mode and Straight Mode - driven by a single actuator, replacing the old DRS concept.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/system/files/documents/fia_2026_f1_regulations_-_section_c_technical_-_iss_20_-_2026-08-05.pdf",
            "publisher": "FIA - 2026 F1 Regulations Section C [Technical] Issue 20",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2026-08-05"
          },
          {
            "url": "https://www.astonmartinf1.com/en-GB/2026",
            "publisher": "Aston Martin Aramco F1 Team",
            "type": "first_party",
            "date": null
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Rear wing profiles are limited to at most three elements, and a failed adjuster must leave the flap in Corner Mode.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/system/files/documents/fia_2026_f1_regulations_-_section_c_technical_-_iss_20_-_2026-08-05.pdf",
            "publisher": "FIA - 2026 F1 Regulations Section C [Technical] Issue 20",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2026-08-05"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "front-suspension": [
      {
        "text": "Suspension must be passive: any powered device that changes suspension configuration is banned, and nothing may be adjusted while the car is moving.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/system/files/documents/fia_2026_f1_regulations_-_section_c_technical_-_iss_20_-_2026-08-05.pdf",
            "publisher": "FIA - 2026 F1 Regulations Section C [Technical] Issue 20",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2026-08-05"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Front and rear suspension must act independently, each responding only to loads on its own axle.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/system/files/documents/fia_2026_f1_regulations_-_section_c_technical_-_iss_20_-_2026-08-05.pdf",
            "publisher": "FIA - 2026 F1 Regulations Section C [Technical] Issue 20",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2026-08-05"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Push-rod vs pull-rod is a team choice; teams pick the layout for both mechanical and aerodynamic reasons.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "url": "https://www.astonmartinf1.com/en-GB/2026",
            "publisher": "Aston Martin Aramco F1 Team",
            "type": "first_party",
            "date": null
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "rear-suspension": [
      {
        "text": "Rear suspension is subject to the same passive-only rule: no powered devices and no in-motion adjustment.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/system/files/documents/fia_2026_f1_regulations_-_section_c_technical_-_iss_20_-_2026-08-05.pdf",
            "publisher": "FIA - 2026 F1 Regulations Section C [Technical] Issue 20",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2026-08-05"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The inboard parts (rockers, springs, dampers) count as sprung mass; uprights, links and wheels are unsprung.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/system/files/documents/fia_2026_f1_regulations_-_section_c_technical_-_iss_20_-_2026-08-05.pdf",
            "publisher": "FIA - 2026 F1 Regulations Section C [Technical] Issue 20",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2026-08-05"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "brakes": [
      {
        "text": "One pedal feeds two master cylinders with separate front and rear hydraulic circuits.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/system/files/documents/fia_2026_f1_regulations_-_section_c_technical_-_iss_20_-_2026-08-05.pdf",
            "publisher": "FIA - 2026 F1 Regulations Section C [Technical] Issue 20",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2026-08-05"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Rear braking pressure may come from a powered brake-by-wire system run by the FIA control electronics, capped at 1.2x the driver's own rear pressure and backed by a hydraulic fallback.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/system/files/documents/fia_2026_f1_regulations_-_section_c_technical_-_iss_20_-_2026-08-05.pdf",
            "publisher": "FIA - 2026 F1 Regulations Section C [Technical] Issue 20",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2026-08-05"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Disc diameter is 325-345 mm at the front and 260-280 mm at the rear, max 34 mm thick; liquid cooling of brakes is forbidden.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/system/files/documents/fia_2026_f1_regulations_-_section_c_technical_-_iss_20_-_2026-08-05.pdf",
            "publisher": "FIA - 2026 F1 Regulations Section C [Technical] Issue 20",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2026-08-05"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "cockpit": [
      {
        "text": "Every car has two roll structures; the secondary one is the halo, built to FIA standard 8869-2018 by an FIA-designated manufacturer.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/system/files/documents/fia_2026_f1_regulations_-_section_c_technical_-_iss_20_-_2026-08-05.pdf",
            "publisher": "FIA - 2026 F1 Regulations Section C [Technical] Issue 20",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2026-08-05"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Roll hoop load requirement rose from 16G to 20G and side intrusion protection was strengthened for 2026.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/news/new-era-competition-fia-showcases-future-focused-formula-1-regulations-2026-and-beyond",
            "publisher": "FIA",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2024-06-06"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Steering re-aligns only the two front wheels and must be a single steering wheel rotating about one axis.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/system/files/documents/fia_2026_f1_regulations_-_section_c_technical_-_iss_20_-_2026-08-05.pdf",
            "publisher": "FIA - 2026 F1 Regulations Section C [Technical] Issue 20",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2026-08-05"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "sidepod": [
      {
        "text": "Primary heat exchangers (radiators) must use aluminium alloy cores and header tanks and cannot be additively manufactured.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/system/files/documents/fia_2026_f1_regulations_-_section_c_technical_-_iss_20_-_2026-08-05.pdf",
            "publisher": "FIA - 2026 F1 Regulations Section C [Technical] Issue 20",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2026-08-05"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "FIA introduced in-washing wheel-wake control boards at the front of the sidepods to manage front-wheel wake.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/news/new-era-competition-fia-showcases-future-focused-formula-1-regulations-2026-and-beyond",
            "publisher": "FIA",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2024-06-06"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "floor": [
      {
        "text": "2026 cars use a partially flat floor and a less powerful diffuser, reducing ground-effect downforce and the need for ultra-stiff, low ride heights.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/news/new-era-competition-fia-showcases-future-focused-formula-1-regulations-2026-and-beyond",
            "publisher": "FIA",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2024-06-06"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Maximum floor width was cut by 150 mm; a plank assembly with three measurement holes runs underneath.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/news/new-era-competition-fia-showcases-future-focused-formula-1-regulations-2026-and-beyond",
            "publisher": "FIA",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2024-06-06"
          },
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/system/files/documents/fia_2026_f1_regulations_-_section_c_technical_-_iss_20_-_2026-08-05.pdf",
            "publisher": "FIA - 2026 F1 Regulations Section C [Technical] Issue 20",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2026-08-05"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "power-unit": [
      {
        "text": "The ICE remains a 1600 cc, 90 deg V6 with four valves per cylinder; fuel energy flow is capped at 3000 MJ/h.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/system/files/documents/fia_2026_f1_regulations_-_section_c_technical_-_iss_20_-_2026-08-05.pdf",
            "publisher": "FIA - 2026 F1 Regulations Section C [Technical] Issue 20",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2026-08-05"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The MGU-H is gone: only the engine and the MGU-K may propel the car or recharge energy. ERS-K power is capped at 350 kW (up from 120 kW).",
        "sources": [
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/system/files/documents/fia_2026_f1_regulations_-_section_c_technical_-_iss_20_-_2026-08-05.pdf",
            "publisher": "FIA - 2026 F1 Regulations Section C [Technical] Issue 20",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2026-08-05"
          },
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/news/new-era-competition-fia-showcases-future-focused-formula-1-regulations-2026-and-beyond",
            "publisher": "FIA",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2024-06-06"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "FIA describes the power split as roughly 50/50: ICE about 400 kW plus 350 kW electric. Recharge is limited to 8.5 MJ per lap and the battery state-of-charge window to 4 MJ.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/news/new-era-competition-fia-showcases-future-focused-formula-1-regulations-2026-and-beyond",
            "publisher": "FIA",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2024-06-06"
          },
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/system/files/documents/fia_2026_f1_regulations_-_section_c_technical_-_iss_20_-_2026-08-05.pdf",
            "publisher": "FIA - 2026 F1 Regulations Section C [Technical] Issue 20",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2026-08-05"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Fuel must be 100% advanced sustainable (from non-food biomass, municipal waste or renewable non-biological feedstock).",
        "sources": [
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/system/files/documents/fia_2026_f1_regulations_-_section_c_technical_-_iss_20_-_2026-08-05.pdf",
            "publisher": "FIA - 2026 F1 Regulations Section C [Technical] Issue 20",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2026-08-05"
          },
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/news/new-era-competition-fia-showcases-future-focused-formula-1-regulations-2026-and-beyond",
            "publisher": "FIA",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2024-06-06"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "front-tyre": [
      {
        "text": "Wheels stay 18-inch (rim diameter ~462.5-463 mm) and must be AZ70/AZ80 magnesium alloy; front rim tyre-mounting width is 315 mm.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/system/files/documents/fia_2026_f1_regulations_-_section_c_technical_-_iss_20_-_2026-08-05.pdf",
            "publisher": "FIA - 2026 F1 Regulations Section C [Technical] Issue 20",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2026-08-05"
          },
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/news/new-era-competition-fia-showcases-future-focused-formula-1-regulations-2026-and-beyond",
            "publisher": "FIA",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2024-06-06"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Front tyres are 25 mm narrower than in 2022-25.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/news/new-era-competition-fia-showcases-future-focused-formula-1-regulations-2026-and-beyond",
            "publisher": "FIA",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2024-06-06"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "rear-tyre": [
      {
        "text": "Rear tyres are 30 mm narrower than in 2022-25; rear rim tyre-mounting width is 401.3 mm.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/news/new-era-competition-fia-showcases-future-focused-formula-1-regulations-2026-and-beyond",
            "publisher": "FIA",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2024-06-06"
          },
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/system/files/documents/fia_2026_f1_regulations_-_section_c_technical_-_iss_20_-_2026-08-05.pdf",
            "publisher": "FIA - 2026 F1 Regulations Section C [Technical] Issue 20",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2026-08-05"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Tyre specification is set by the supplier with the FIA; teams may not cut, groove or chemically treat tyres.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/system/files/documents/fia_2026_f1_regulations_-_section_c_technical_-_iss_20_-_2026-08-05.pdf",
            "publisher": "FIA - 2026 F1 Regulations Section C [Technical] Issue 20",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2026-08-05"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "dimensions": [
      {
        "text": "Maximum wheelbase is 3400 mm (down from 3600 mm) and maximum width 1900 mm (down from 2000 mm).",
        "sources": [
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/system/files/documents/fia_2026_f1_regulations_-_section_c_technical_-_iss_20_-_2026-08-05.pdf",
            "publisher": "FIA - 2026 F1 Regulations Section C [Technical] Issue 20",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2026-08-05"
          },
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/news/new-era-competition-fia-showcases-future-focused-formula-1-regulations-2026-and-beyond",
            "publisher": "FIA",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2024-06-06"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Minimum mass is set as a car+driver figure plus Pirelli's measured nominal tyre mass: 724 kg (726 kg in qualifying) + tyres under Issue 20. The 2024 launch figure was 768 kg (722 kg + ~46 kg tyres).",
        "sources": [
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/system/files/documents/fia_2026_f1_regulations_-_section_c_technical_-_iss_20_-_2026-08-05.pdf",
            "publisher": "FIA - 2026 F1 Regulations Section C [Technical] Issue 20",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2026-08-05"
          },
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/news/new-era-competition-fia-showcases-future-focused-formula-1-regulations-2026-and-beyond",
            "publisher": "FIA",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2024-06-06"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The gearbox must have exactly eight forward ratios; CVTs are banned.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "url": "https://api.fia.com/system/files/documents/fia_2026_f1_regulations_-_section_c_technical_-_iss_20_-_2026-08-05.pdf",
            "publisher": "FIA - 2026 F1 Regulations Section C [Technical] Issue 20",
            "type": "fia",
            "date": "2026-08-05"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
